/// Chapter 43 of the guide, written from md-docs/errors/diagnostics.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page ErrorsGuide(path: "/errors", title: "Diagnostics", description: "Every WebFluent error and warning, by code — what it means, a program that draws it, the message the compiler prints, and the fix.", layout: DocsShell("Diagnostics", chapter: t("nav.group.reference"), blurb: "Every error and warning the compiler reports — what it means, a program that draws it, the message, and the fix.", source: "md-docs/errors/diagnostics.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "reading-a-finding", label: "Reading a finding"), Anchor(id: "errors-and-warnings", label: "Errors and warnings"), Anchor(id: "findings-for-a-tool", label: "Findings for a tool"), Anchor(id: "fixes", label: "Fixes"), Anchor(id: "changing-what-a-finding-counts-as", label: "Changing what a finding counts as"), Anchor(id: "allowing-one-finding", label: "Allowing one finding"), Anchor(id: "explaining-a-code", label: "Explaining a code"), Anchor(id: "the-families", label: "The families"), Anchor(id: "every-code", label: "Every code")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/config", prevLabel: t("ch.42"), nextTo: "/docs/guide/built-ins", nextLabel: t("ch.44"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This chapter is the reference for every finding the compiler reports. Each finding has a code, such as `T05`, and each code has a page of its own, listed below; `wf explain T05` prints the same entry in your terminal.\n\n`wf build`, `wf check`, `wf serve` and your editor report the same findings, from one pipeline. This chapter first explains how to read a finding and how to change what one counts as, then lists every code by family.")

        Heading("Reading a finding", id: "reading-a-finding").h2

        Markdown("Every finding is printed in the same layout. This one reports a misspelt field:")

        CodeBlock(#"error[T05]: `User` has no field `nmae`
 --> src/pages/Profile.wf:3:18
  |
3 |     Heading(user.nmae).h1
  |                  ^^^^
  = help: Its fields are `id`, `name`
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/T05"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("From the top, a finding shows:\n\n1. its severity, its code and what is wrong;\n2. the place, in the `file:line:col` form that editors and CI problem matchers read;\n3. the line of source, with the part that is wrong underlined;\n4. `help:` — what to do about it, when the compiler can say;\n5. `docs:` — a link to the code's entry in this chapter.\n\nColour is used only on a terminal, and never when `NO_COLOR` is set.")

        Heading("Errors and warnings", id: "errors-and-warnings").h2

        Markdown("Every code has a severity:\n\n- An **error** stops the build: the program cannot mean what it says.\n- A **warning** prints and the build goes on: the program means something, probably not what you wanted. Nothing is a warning that the compiler could have decided for itself.\n\nEvery stage of the compiler runs on whatever the stage before it found, and every file is read even when another does not parse — the parser picks up again at the next declaration. One build therefore shows every mistake once, then sums them up in one line: `error: the build stopped: 2 errors, 5 warnings`.\n\nA build that stops on its findings exits with `1`. A build that cannot run at all — a file it cannot read, a config it cannot load — exits with `2`. `--deny-warnings` on `wf build` or `wf check` makes a warning stop the build too.")

        Heading("Findings for a tool", id: "findings-for-a-tool").h2

        Markdown("`--format` on `wf build` and `wf check` writes the same findings for a tool ([Command line](/docs/guide/cli#wf-check)):")

        Table(caption: "Findings for a tool") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Format").header
                    Table.Cell("Output").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`json`") }
                    Table.Cell("One document on standard output, with every finding's code, place, hint, related places and fixes.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sarif`") }
                    Table.Cell("SARIF 2.1.0, for GitHub code scanning.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`github`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`::error` annotations, which a GitHub workflow shows on the pull request.") }
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Fixes", id: "fixes").h2

        Markdown("Where the compiler knows the fix, the finding carries it as edits. Your editor offers it as a quick fix, `--format json` carries it in `fixes`, and [`wf fix`](/docs/guide/cli#wf-fix) applies it. A fix is offered only where it is certain; where it is not, the code's entry says what to do instead.\n\nEach kind of finding has its decided fix:\n\n- **The nearest name**, wherever the code names a set: a field, member, method, variable, component, case or flag (`T02`, `T05`, `T06`, `T13`, `T16`, `E101`, `E103`), a prop (`C02`, `C04`), a route (`R01`, which also rewrites a relative link from the root), a store (`X05`), a locale (`I04`), a file of `public/` (`D01`), a CSS property or token (`V05`, `V06`), an icon (`V08`) and an event (`V09`).\n- **What is missing, written in**: `?.` for a read that may be null (`T04`), `(await …)` for a promise read as its value (`T17`), the missing props (`C01`), the missing arms of a `match` (`T15`) and an `error` arm (`T21`), a `Router` in an `app` with none (`R03`), `bind:` for a box that shows a state and never changes it (`F04`), `px` for a bare number where CSS wants a length (`V07`), `controls: true` (`A09`), and the `migrate` step a version is missing (`P01`) — with the version raised in the same change when a persisted shape changed (`D04`).\n- **A name, drafted from the code**: `alt: \"\"` for an image (`A01`); a label from what a control binds or what an icon is (`A02`–`A04`), a link's from where it leads (`A06`), a dialog's title from what opens it (`A08`); the heading level that mends the outline (`A11`); the visible text at the start of an `aria-label` (`A15`). With nothing to draft from, there is no fix, because an empty name would silence the warning and name nothing.\n- **What is not used, removed** — a state, derived value, action, store member or component (`U01`–`U05`), code after a `return` (`U06`), an allow that allows nothing (`U07`) — with *rename to `_name`* as the second fix, for what you keep on purpose; and a loop keyed `by item.id` when its body reads the item's `id` (`U09`).\n- **A change of form**: `derived` for a state that copies a live value nothing changes (`X06`), a positional argument named for the one prop it can be (`C05`), and the prop marked `_` in the component's declaration (`C06`).\n\nA family's findings in one file are fixed together, as one change: the editor's **Fix all `V07` in this file**, or `wf fix --code V07` for the whole project.")

        Heading("Changing what a finding counts as", id: "changing-what-a-finding-counts-as").h2

        Markdown("`lints` in `webfluent.app.json` sets what a finding counts as for the whole project, by code or by family — `\"off\"`, `\"warn\"` or `\"error\"`. A code's setting wins over its family's:")

        CodeBlock(#"{ "lints": { "A11": "off", "U": "error", "R01": "warn" } }"#, title: "json")

        Markdown("You can turn any warning off or raise it to an error. You can lower an error only when it cannot ship a broken page: `R01`, `C02`, `S04`, `I01`, `I02` and `I04`. Lowering any other error is refused ([Configuration](/docs/guide/config#lints)).")

        Heading("Allowing one finding", id: "allowing-one-finding").h2

        Markdown("To accept one finding on purpose, write a `// wf-allow(CODE)` comment:\n\n- on a line of its own, it covers the next line of code;\n- at the end of a line, it covers that line.\n\nIt names codes or families, comma-separated — `// wf-allow(U01, A)`. Only a finding that [`lints`](/docs/guide/config#lints) could lower may be allowed. An allow that covers nothing is itself reported (`U07`), so an allow does not outlive what it was for.")

        Heading("Explaining a code", id: "explaining-a-code").h2

        Markdown("`wf explain CODE` prints a code's entry from this chapter, word for word; `wf explain` with no code lists every code with its severity and title.")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf explain T05"),
                Line(command: "wf explain")
            ])

        Heading("The families", id: "the-families").h2

        Markdown("A code's letter is its family:")

        Table(caption: "The families") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Family").header
                    Table.Cell("What it covers").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`E`") }
                    Table.Cell("syntax and structure: what cannot be read, or refers to nothing")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`T`") }
                    Table.Cell("types")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`C`") }
                    Table.Cell("components and their props")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`R`") }
                    Table.Cell("routes and navigation")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`X`") }
                    Table.Cell("state and reactivity")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`I`") }
                    Table.Cell("translations")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`F`") }
                    Table.Cell("forms and bindings")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`D`") }
                    Table.Cell("data, assets and what is kept in the browser")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`A`") }
                    Table.Cell("accessibility")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`S`") }
                    Table.Cell("search and sharing")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`P`") }
                    Table.Cell("persisted values")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`U`") }
                    Table.Cell("declared and never used")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`V`") }
                    Table.Cell("vocabulary")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Each code's page has the same parts: the code and its title as the heading, what it means, a program that draws it, the message the compiler prints for that program, and the fix. The test suite compiles every example program, checks that it draws exactly the code it is filed under, and checks that the message shown is what the compiler prints.")

        Heading("Every code", id: "every-code").h2

        Heading("Syntax and structure", id: "syntax-and-structure").h3

        Markdown("Errors, except where an entry says otherwise.\n\n- [E001](/errors/E001) — Text the compiler cannot read\n- [E002](/errors/E002) — A syntax error\n- [E003](/errors/E003) — Indentation that lines up with no block\n- [E004](/errors/E004) — A file in the WebFluent 2 grammar\n- [E005](/errors/E005) — A file the formatter will not change\n- [E101](/errors/E101) — A component nothing declares\n- [E102](/errors/E102) — A name declared twice\n- [E103](/errors/E103) — A flag, case, part, event or slot the component does not have\n- [E104](/errors/E104) — A layout with nowhere to put the page\n- [E105](/errors/E105) — A statement a render block cannot hold\n- [E106](/errors/E106) — Script or a whole style in an attribute\n- [E107](/errors/E107) — A URL a browser would run\n- [E108](/errors/E108) — An `env` name that is not public\n- [E109](/errors/E109) — An element this output cannot draw\n- [E110](/errors/E110) — A project script that cannot be a plain script\n- [E111](/errors/E111) — A setting that cannot work\n- [E112](/errors/E112) — A setting nothing reads\n- [E113](/errors/E113) — An argument that cannot be positional\n- [E114](/errors/E114) — `emit` outside a component\n- [E115](/errors/E115) — A project script the compiler could not read\n- [E116](/errors/E116) — A tag that cannot be a custom element's\n- [E117](/errors/E117) — A key combination no keyboard sends\n- [E118](/errors/E118) — A name the language already has\n- [E901](/errors/E901) — The compiler wrote JavaScript a browser would refuse\n- [E902](/errors/E902) — Output its own security policy refuses\n- [E119](/errors/E119) — A hidden direction control in the source\n- [E120](/errors/E120) — Something nests too deeply\n- [E121](/errors/E121) — A render that would do too much")

        Heading("Types", id: "types").h3

        Markdown("Errors. The type checker's findings; a program that declares no types raises none of them, since what it cannot resolve is `Any`.\n\n- [T01](/errors/T01) — A value of the wrong type\n- [T02](/errors/T02) — A case the enum does not have\n- [T04](/errors/T04) — A value that may be null, read as if it were not\n- [T05](/errors/T05) — A field or method that does not exist\n- [T06](/errors/T06) — A member a store or service does not have\n- [T07](/errors/T07) — A condition that is always true\n- [T08](/errors/T08) — A loop over something that is not a list\n- [T09](/errors/T09) — An `emit` that does not match its event\n- [T10](/errors/T10) — A call with the wrong arguments\n- [T11](/errors/T11) — A `match` on something that cannot be matched\n- [T12](/errors/T12) — A secret where it would escape\n- [T13](/errors/T13) — A name nothing declares\n- [T16](/errors/T16) — A method a number, a string or a list does not have\n- [T14](/errors/T14) — A comparison that is always the same\n- [T17](/errors/T17) — An async result used before it is awaited\n- [T19](/errors/T19) — A value that may be null, shown as text\n- [T20](/errors/T20) — A list or a record shown as text\n- [T18](/errors/T18) — Arithmetic on something that is not a number\n- [T15](/errors/T15) — A `match` that misses a case, or has one twice\n- [T22](/errors/T22) — A handler that names more values than its event sends\n- [T21](/errors/T21) — A resource `match` with no `error` arm")

        Heading("Components", id: "components").h3

        Markdown("- [C01](/errors/C01) — A required prop or field left out\n- [C02](/errors/C02) — A prop the component does not declare\n- [C03](/errors/C03) — A part outside the component it belongs to\n- [C04](/errors/C04) — An attribute a built-in does not declare\n- [C05](/errors/C05) — A positional argument a built-in does not take\n- [C06](/errors/C06) — A positional argument bound by order\n- [C07](/errors/C07) — A drag or a gesture on a component with no one element")

        Heading("Routes", id: "routes").h3

        Markdown("- [R01](/errors/R01) — A route to nothing\n- [R02](/errors/R02) — A route parameter and a page parameter that do not match\n- [R03](/errors/R03) — An `app` with no `Router`, or with two\n- [R04](/errors/R04) — A relative URL on a nested route\n- [R05](/errors/R05) — A translation of no page, or two in one language")

        Heading("State and reactivity", id: "state-and-reactivity").h3

        Markdown("- [X01](/errors/X01) — An assignment to something that cannot change\n- [X02](/errors/X02) — An effect that feeds itself\n- [X04](/errors/X04) — A derived value that changes something\n- [X05](/errors/X05) — `use` of a store nothing declares\n- [X06](/errors/X06) — A state that copies a live value once")

        Heading("Forms and bindings", id: "forms-and-bindings").h3

        Markdown("- [F01](/errors/F01) — A `bind:` to something that cannot be written\n- [F02](/errors/F02) — A `bind:` to a state the control cannot hold\n- [F03](/errors/F03) — A `validate` block no control can satisfy\n- [F04](/errors/F04) — A checkbox that shows a state and never changes it\n- [F05](/errors/F05) — A select whose value is none of its options")

        Heading("Data and assets", id: "data-and-assets").h3

        Markdown("- [D01](/errors/D01) — A file the project does not have\n- [D02](/errors/D02) — A persisted value storage cannot keep\n- [D03](/errors/D03) — A persisted value every instance shares\n- [D04](/errors/D04) — A persisted shape changed with no new version\n- [D05](/errors/D05) — An asset from another origin with no integrity hash")

        Heading("Translations", id: "translations").h3

        Markdown("These need the project's translation files, so the examples are described rather than run.\n\n- [I01](/errors/I01) — A message no translation has\n- [I02](/errors/I02) — A message and its call that disagree\n- [I03](/errors/I03) — A message one locale has and another does not\n- [I04](/errors/I04) — A locale the project does not have\n- [I05](/errors/I05) — Words a reader sees that are not translated")

        Heading("Accessibility", id: "accessibility").h3

        Markdown("Warnings. What makes a page unusable with a screen reader, a keyboard or a voice.\n\n- [A01](/errors/A01) — An image with no alt text\n- [A02](/errors/A02) — An icon button with no name\n- [A03](/errors/A03) — An input with no label\n- [A04](/errors/A04) — A control with no label\n- [A05](/errors/A05) — A button with no text\n- [A06](/errors/A06) — A link with no text\n- [A07](/errors/A07) — An empty heading\n- [A08](/errors/A08) — A dialog with no title\n- [A09](/errors/A09) — Media nobody can follow without sound\n- [A10](/errors/A10) — A table with no header row\n- [A11](/errors/A11) — A skipped heading level\n- [A12](/errors/A12) — A page without exactly one h1\n- [A13](/errors/A13) — Colours without enough contrast\n- [A14](/errors/A14) — A role whose children are the wrong kind\n- [A15](/errors/A15) — An `aria-label` that does not contain the visible text\n- [A16](/errors/A16) — One id on several elements\n- [A17](/errors/A17) — A frame with no title")

        Heading("Search and sharing", id: "search-and-sharing").h3

        Markdown("Warnings. What a search engine or a link preview would act on.\n\n- [S01](/errors/S01) — A page with no title\n- [S02](/errors/S02) — A page with no description\n- [S03](/errors/S03) — A description too long for a search result\n- [S04](/errors/S04) — Two pages on one route")

        Heading("What is kept in the browser", id: "what-is-kept-in-the-browser").h3

        Markdown("Warnings. `persist` values across releases.\n\n- [P01](/errors/P01) — A persisted value with no way forward\n- [P02](/errors/P02) — A migration that never runs\n- [P03](/errors/P03) — A persisted value in a route-scoped store")

        Heading("Declared and never read", id: "declared-and-never-read").h3

        Markdown("Warnings. A name beginning `_` is taken as unused on purpose.\n\n- [U01](/errors/U01) — A state nothing reads\n- [U02](/errors/U02) — A derived value nothing reads\n- [U03](/errors/U03) — A component nothing places\n- [U04](/errors/U04) — A store member nothing reads\n- [U05](/errors/U05) — An action nothing calls\n- [U06](/errors/U06) — Code after return\n- [U07](/errors/U07) — An allow that allows nothing\n- [U08](/errors/U08) — A condition that is always the same\n- [U09](/errors/U09) — An unkeyed loop whose items hold state\n- [U10](/errors/U10) — An `else` no value reaches")

        Heading("Vocabulary", id: "vocabulary").h3

        Markdown("Warnings.\n\n- [V01](/errors/V01) — A bare word that means nothing\n- [V02](/errors/V02) — A flag no stylesheet styles\n- [V03](/errors/V03) — Markup put in as markup\n- [V04](/errors/V04) — A class that is the engine's\n- [V05](/errors/V05) — A CSS property no browser knows\n- [V06](/errors/V06) — A design token the theme does not declare\n- [V07](/errors/V07) — A number where CSS wants a length\n- [V08](/errors/V08) — An icon the runtime does not draw\n- [V09](/errors/V09) — An event the element does not fire\n- [V12](/errors/V12) — A long list that is not windowed\n- [V10](/errors/V10) — A `Host` tag it does not make\n- [V11](/errors/V11) — A component named like a built-in")
    }
}
